---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

// Every credential on this page comes from the Brand Guide's "Core Proof Bank"
// (section 11), which lists what is safe to publish in evergreen copy. Claims
// the guide flags for verification first -- named clients, stage counts,
// audience totals, outcome percentages -- are deliberately absent. Do not add
// one without checking permission and wording against the guide.
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Imagination Applied brings Artistic Intelligence into organizations through live experiences, executive advisory, and rehearsal-based transformation. Founded by Josh Penzell."
  path="/about/"
>
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>A company built on rehearsal</h1>
    <p class="lede">{SITE.description}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap page-body">
    <p>{SITE.boilerplate}</p>

    <div class="section-rule">
      <h2>Why theater</h2>
      <p>
        The premise is not that business should be more creative. It is that organizations
        already face the exact conditions a director works in every day: the material is
        incomplete, several interpretations are possible, judgment matters more than
        compliance, and the right answer changes as the work moves.
      </p>
      <p>
        Theater has spent a few thousand years developing a craft for exactly that. Most
        management practice has not. So we borrow the craft rather than the vocabulary—and
        when the theater language stops doing real work, we drop it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section-rule">
      <h2>Josh Penzell, founder</h2>
      <p>
        Josh Penzell helps leaders create direction when the answer is not waiting to be
        found. He is a keynote speaker, advisor, founder of Imagination Applied, and
        forthcoming author of <em>Artistic Intelligence</em>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Trained as a theater director and formerly VP of AI Innovation &amp; Strategy at
        ELB Learning, Josh brings the rehearsal room into the future of work—helping
        organizations align people, direct AI, and turn uncertainty into intelligent
        action. He has worked across learning and enablement in organizations including
        Amazon Alexa and Skillsoft, holds an MFA in Theater Directing from Brooklyn
        College and a BS from Northwestern University, and writes for TD Magazine.
      </p>
      <p>
        His keynotes are live, participatory, and built around a simple idea: AI does not
        replace leadership. It changes what leadership has to rehearse for.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href={SITE.founderSite}>joshpenzell.com →</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="section-rule">
      <h2>How the pieces fit</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt><strong>Artistic Intelligence</strong></dt>
        <dd class="muted" style="margin:0 0 1rem">
          The philosophy and the capacity. The subject of Josh's forthcoming book.
        </dd>
        <dt><strong>TheaterThink</strong></dt>
        <dd class="muted" style="margin:0 0 1rem">
          The rehearsal-based practice. How the philosophy is actually run.
        </dd>
        <dt><strong>Imagination Applied</strong></dt>
        <dd class="muted" style="margin:0 0 1rem">
          The company. Where the work becomes engagements and organizational change.
        </dd>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="section-rule">
      <h2>What we publish</h2>
      <p>
        We publish research under the <a href="/publications/">Open Research Series</a>,
        with the analysis code and file checksums released alongside each paper. The
        standard we hold ourselves to is simple: every claim traceable to code, and
        limitations stated in the body rather than a footnote.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Start a conversation</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={SITE.linkedin}>Follow on LinkedIn</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
